    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to satisfy the identity-key-v2 specification.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` now returns the **SHA-256 hex digest** over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (a 64-char lower-case hex string), replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` join. The third parameter is now `lastName` instead of `householdId`.\n- `getIdentityKey()` feeds `this.telephone`, `this.email`, `this.lastName`.\n- Added a standard **American Soundex** implementation (`soundex` + `soundexCode` helper): retained first letter, digit-coded consonants, vowels/Y as separators, H/W transparent, adjacent same-code collapse, zero-padded to 4.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` now keys 409 detection on the single identity key across **all non-deleted owners** \u2014 the `householdId`-based gating and `householdMembers` scoping are gone. The email-domain blocklist still runs first (via `normalizeEmail` earlier in the pipeline), and `sharesHousehold` still bypasses.\n- `findPossibleDuplicate` (soft match) now triggers when the **identity key differs** but **soundex(lastName)** and **postcode** match \u2014 so two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are a soft match, not a 409.\n- Updated the surrounding javadoc on `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, `findPossibleDuplicate`, and `applyPossibleDuplicate` to describe the new behaviour.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` field description/example to the hashed v2 form.\n\nThe household helpers (`householdIdFor`, `assignHousehold`, `householdMembers`, etc.) remain \u2014 they're still used for membership-level caps and household member counts \u2014 they're just no longer part of duplicate detection.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
